-# locals: set_id (String)
-#
-# The Set edit page's Visibility tab: one bulk action that strips public read
-# from every Work the set holds.
-#
-# The tab is "Visibility" and the action names itself fully, because there is
-# deliberately no matching "make public" and a tab called "Privatize" would
-# imply its inverse sits somewhere nearby. The absence is stated on the pane
-# rather than left for someone to go looking for: a one-click widening across a
-# whole set is a disclosure foot-gun, and the reason is more useful to the
-# reader than the silence.
-#
-# The work count is the lazily-loaded frame the My Sets index already uses, so
-# the blast radius is on the screen before the button is pressed without the
-# edit page paying a recipe resolution on every load.
.py-2.px-1
  .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
    %h5.mb-1 Visibility
    %p.small.text-muted.mb-0
      Remove public access from every work this set holds. Group grants are kept, so a work stays
      readable by the groups it already names — and those grants are what it falls back on. Works
      that are already private are left alone.

  .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
    .d-flex.align-items-baseline.gap-2.mb-1
      %h6.mb-0 This set currently holds
      = turbo_frame_tag "set-works-count-#{set_id}", src: works_count_set_path(set_id), loading: :lazy do
        %span.text-muted Counting…
    %p.small.text-muted.mb-0
      The sweep covers the works the set resolves to right now, including those it reaches through
      an included collection. Works you have set aside are not touched.

  -# The warning sits before the control it applies to, not under it.
  .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
    %h6.mb-1
      %i.fa-solid.fa-triangle-exclamation.text-danger.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
      This cannot be undone
    %p.small.text-muted.mb-3
      There is no bulk action to make works public again. Restoring public access means editing each
      work, so check the set's contents before you run this. A work removed from the set afterwards
      stays private.
    = button_to privatize_set_path(set_id), class: "btn btn-danger", form: { class: "d-inline" },
                data: { turbo_confirm: "Make every work in this set private? Public access is removed from all of them. There is no bulk action to undo this.",
                        turbo_confirm_title: "Confirm privatize",
                        turbo_confirm_button: "Make private",
                        turbo_confirm_variant: "danger" } do
      %i.fa-solid.fa-user-lock.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
      Make all works private
